    "content": "The Somali Future Council (Golaha Mustaqbalka Soomaaliya), a coalition of former presidents, Puntland officials, and civil society representatives, has formally requested that Somalia revert to its transitional governance structure. The proposal aims to tackle ongoing political and security crises that have impeded progress toward a permanent federal system.\n\nFormed earlier this year, the council argues that the current federal framework has failed to deliver effective governance, particularly in regions plagued by conflict and weak state institutions. Its members include notable figures such as former President Sharif Sheikh Ahmed and Puntland President Said Abdullahi Deni, who have voiced support for a return to a consensus-based interim arrangement.\n\nThe call echoes previous efforts to establish a more inclusive political process, with the council emphasizing the need for dialogue among all stakeholders. This comes amid renewed violence from Al-Shabaab and delays in electoral reforms, which have heightened concerns about Somalia's stability.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development is significant as it could influence the political landscape in the homeland. Many diaspora members have advocated for effective governance to enable safe return and investment. The council's proposal may spark debate on how best to achieve lasting peace and development.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/golaha-mustaqbalka-oo-dalbaday-in-somalia-lagu-celiyo-hanaankii-kumeel-gaarka/424205/",
